  "notes": "{喚|わめ}く implies loud, uncontrolled shouting or screaming, often with a negative connotation suggesting the person is being unreasonable, hysterical, or obnoxious.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {自動詞|じどうし} (intransitive)\n- No transitive pair\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {大声|おおごえ}で{喚|わめ}く: to scream at the top of one's lungs\n- {泣|な}き{喚|わめ}く: to cry and scream (compound verb)\n- {喚|わめ}き{散|ち}らす: to scream wildly, make a scene\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {叫|さけ}ぶ: to shout, to scream (more neutral, can be positive)\n- {怒鳴|どな}る: to yell angrily (specifically angry tone)\n- {騒|さわ}ぐ: to make noise, be rowdy (broader meaning)\n\nREGISTER:\n{喚|わめ}く carries a strongly negative nuance. Using it to describe someone implies disapproval of their behavior.",
